{"Django QuerySets do not support negative indexing. When `enable_advanced_features` is True and `cursor.offset < 0`, `start_offset` will be negative, and `queryset[start_offset:stop]` will raise `AssertionError: Negative indexing is not supported.` at runtime.": 0.9861559271812439, "`OptimizedCursorPaginator.get_item_key` calls `math.floor()`/`math.ceil()` directly on a `datetime` value (since `order_by=\"-datetime\"`). Unlike `DateTimePaginator`, it does not convert the datetime to a numeric timestamp first, so this will raise `TypeError` at runtime.": 0.9796026945114136, "Switching `span-buf:s:*` from SADD to ZADD without a migration means a rolling deploy will hit WRONGTYPE errors for any existing Set keys, dropping spans until those keys expire. Consider migrating/renaming keys or deleting non-zset keys before writing.": 0.9329447150230408, "`organization_context.member` can be `None` (documented in the model), so accessing `.has_global_access` will raise `AttributeError` when the user is not a superuser and has no membership.": 0.7729856371879578, "Comments about 'performance optimization' and 'negative offset support' in cursors.py are misleading: no code was changed on that line, so there is no new negative-offset support being introduced. These comments can mislead future maintainers.": 0.5637246370315552, "`self.max_segment_spans` is now dead code. Its only usage was the span-count guard in `_load_segment_data`, which this PR removes. The parameter and attribute should be cleaned up to avoid confusion.": 0.48202693462371826, "ZUNIONSTORE defaults to AGGREGATE SUM, which will add timestamp scores when the same span payload exists in both sets. Since scores are end timestamps, this can distort ordering and eviction. Specify AGGREGATE MAX (or MIN) to preserve the original timestamp when merging.": 0.9803712368011475}